   <!-- Expected values for validation (2025) -->
   <!-- Income: $75,000 + $55,000 W-2 = $130,000 -->
   <!-- Federal: AGI $130,000; standard deduction $31,500 (MFJ; 2025 after OBBBA, P.L. 119-21 sec. 70102; IRS IR-2025-103); taxable income
        $130,000 - $31,500 = $98,500; tax $11,498 (2025 MFJ schedule, Rev. Proc. 2024-40) -->
   <!-- Child tax credit 2 x $2,200 = $4,400 (2025, IRC 24(h)); tax after credit $7,098 -->
   <!-- Missouri (2025 Form MO-1040 and 2025 Tax Chart, dor.mo.gov): line 11 federal tax is
        Form 1040 line 22 (after nonrefundable credits), $7,098; line 12 percentage for
        Missouri AGI $130,000 is 0%; line 13 federal income tax deduction $0 (cap $5,000/$10,000);
        line 14 standard deduction $31,500 -->
   <!-- Combined return: line 7 income percentages 58% / 42% (rounded to a whole percent);
        line 26 $130,000 - $0 - $31,500 = $98,500; line 27Y $57,130, 27S $41,370; chart: Y $256 + 4.7% of
        $47,939 = $2,509, S $256 + 4.7% of $32,179 = $1,768; line 30 total $4,277 -->
   <!-- expected_state_tax was $4525, not derived from the state's 2025 form (#1317). -->
